sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Pyramid Fuzz audio callback sequence
    accDescr: Preparation allocates all quality paths and buffers before playback. Each non-empty callback samples parameter atomics once, updates the engine, and processes bounded chunks. Each chunk captures delayed dry audio, runs the selected oversampled wet circuit and applies bypass blending. Mono duplication and atomic peak publication occur before returning audio. UI meter polling is independent.
    participant H as Host / JUCE wrapper
    participant P as PluginProcessor
    participant A as APVTS
    participant E as FuzzEngine
    participant O as OversamplingEngine
    participant N as Selected NonlinearPath

    Note over H,N: Before playback: prepare all samplers, paths and buffers / initialize state / report six-sample latency
    Note over H,N: Audio thread — one non-empty host callback
    H->>P: processBlock() or processBlockBypassed()
    activate P
    P->>P: Input peak / clear extra outputs
    P->>A: readParameters() — atomic loads
    A-->>P: Eight current parameter values
    P->>E: updateParameters(snapshot)
    Note over E,O: Smoothing targets and quality handover at this callback boundary

    loop Each chunk ≤ prepared block size
        P->>P: Capture sanitized dry audio, delayed six samples
        P->>E: processBlock(chunk) — even during host bypass
        activate E
        E->>E: Advance host-rate control smoothers
        E->>O: processBlock(chunk, circuit callback)
        activate O
        O->>O: Filtered upsampling
        O->>E: Invoke circuit callback
        loop Each oversampled sample and input channel
            E->>N: process(channel, sample, controls)
            N-->>E: Wet circuit sample
        end
        Note over E,N: Hold each host-rate control value across its oversampled sample group
        E-->>O: Circuit callback returns
        O->>O: Downsample + latency padding
        O-->>E: Host-rate wet audio
        deactivate O
        E->>E: 1/3 scale × Volume × quality fade
        E-->>P: Wet chunk
        deactivate E
        P->>P: Aligned dry/wet blend, 5 ms bypass ramp
    end

    P->>P: Mono duplication / output peak
    P->>P: Publish PeakMeter atomics
    P-->>H: Processed audio buffer
    deactivate P
    Note over H,N: Editor polls meters at 30 Hz independently — no UI calls in this callback
